text:
A.
Findings:
The town council finds that the health, safety, and general welfare of the citizens of Basin will be best served by dividing the town into various zoning districts or zones and regulating the erection, construction, reconstruction, alteration, repair or use of buildings, structures on the land within these zones.
The zoning regulations of this title shall be designed to accomplish the statutorily authorized purposes of:
1. Securing safety from fire, panic, and other dangers;
2. Providing adequate light and air;
3. Preventing the overcrowding of land;
4. Avoiding undue concentration of population;
5. Facilitating adequate provisions for transportation, water, sewerage, electrical power, schools, parks and other public requirements;
6. Conserving the value of buildings and encouraging the most appropriate use of land throughout the city or town; and
7. Preserving, rehabilitating and maintaining historic properties and encouraging compatible uses.
B. Scope:
The town council, acting in light of the above findings, does hereby resolve that this title shall govern all erection, construction, reconstruction, alteration, repair or use of buildings, structures or land within the town dependent on the availability of a code enforcer.
(Ord.
685, 11-12-2020)
